        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Van", "{DL} says it was a campaign van.")],
        role: "Candidate",
        exam: [.direct("What did you learn about your campaign's money?", "\"Our treasurer, {D}, paid $31,000 to a car dealership out of donations. The campaign filing, thirty days later, listed it as signage.\""), .direct("What did the dealership invoice show?", "\"A sedan titled to {D.him}. Not a campaign van, and not signage.\""), .direct("Did you buy a van?", "\"No. No van was bought. I never authorized a vehicle purchase with campaign money.\""), .direct("What was your role in the campaign?", "\"I was the candidate, running for county commissioner. {D.He} volunteered to be my treasurer and handled the bank account and the filings.\""), .direct("Who authorized the payment?", "\"The treasurer signed alone. The campaign's rules required two signatures, and only one was on the check.\""), .direct("What did you do then?", "\"I asked {D.him} for the paperwork. The invoice showed a sedan titled to {D.him}, and I removed {D.him} as treasurer that day.\""), .cross("{DL} says it was a campaign van, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"We did rent a van at one point. But the invoice shows a sedan in {D.his} name.\""), .cross("Did you review the filings yourself?", "\"I relied on {DL} as treasurer. I looked at the totals. I didn't check each line, and I own that.\""), .cross("Did {DL} tell you about the car?", "\"No. Never. I learned from the invoice. {D.He} never told me.\""), .cross("The campaign did rent a van at one point, didn't it?", "\"Yes, for a few weekends at a lower cost. I never approved a van purchase.\""), .cross("You signed the campaign's reports too, didn't you?", "\"I signed as candidate, based on what {D.he} provided. I did not check the line items against receipts.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Campaign volunteer",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What was your role in the campaign?", "\"I volunteered at events, put up signs, and drove people to polls. I worked about fifteen hours a week for four months.\""), .direct("How did the campaign move people and supplies?", "\"Mostly in a rented white van that we picked up on weekends. Volunteers took turns driving.\""), .direct("Did you know about a van purchase?", "\"No. I never heard anyone say the campaign bought a van. We just kept renting.\""), .direct("What did you see {D} doing?", "\"Paying bills and taking calls from vendors. {D} was always at the office on Tuesday nights doing paperwork.\""), .direct("What vehicle did the defendant drive?", "\"A newer gray sedan that I noticed shortly after the money came in. I assumed it was a personal car.\""), .direct("What was the mood in the office when this came out?", "\"Shocked. The candidate was angry, and we all felt let down.\""), .cross("You do not know where the $31,000 went, do you?", "\"I do not. I only know about the rented van.\""), .cross("The sedan was not a campaign vehicle, was it?", "\"As far as I know, it was not used for signs or volunteers.\""), .cross("You never saw receipts for a purchase, did you?", "\"No. I never saw any paperwork about it.\""), .cross("You never asked the defendant about the car, did you?", "\"No. It was none of my business, and I assumed it belonged to {D.him}.\""), .cross("The rented van cost much less than $31,000, didn't it?", "\"Much less. I think the rental was a few hundred dollars a weekend.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} bought a car.", "A campaign van."),
        allocution: "\"I meant that vehicle for campaign events and travel, and I listed it as signage by mistake. The dealership wrote it up in my name, and I had no idea it would be titled to me. I never meant to take donor money, and I'll make it right.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} drove the sedan daily.", "The campaign did use a rented van."),
        defendant: [.direct("What did you buy with $31,000?", "\"A vehicle for the campaign. I meant it to be used for events and travel. I listed it as signage by mistake.\""), .direct("Why does the invoice say sedan?", "\"The dealership wrote it up that way. I had no idea it would be titled to me. It was supposed to be for the campaign.\""), .direct("Did you use it for yourself?", "\"Some. I drove it for campaign business and sometimes personal. I didn't think it was wrong.\""), .direct("What did the campaign need?", "\"A reliable vehicle to carry signs, volunteers, and supplies across the county. The rented van was unreliable and cost too much.\""), .direct("How did you make the purchase?", "\"I thought I was buying a vehicle for the campaign, and the dealership prepared the title in my name for convenience. I meant to transfer it later.\""), .direct("Why was it filed as signage?", "\"I made a bad coding choice when I was in a hurry and did not know a better category. A better category would have stayed with a person who read the rules.\""), .cross("The sedan is titled to you, isn't it?", "\"Yes. The dealer did the title that way. I should have checked.\""), .cross("The filing says signage, doesn't it?", "\"Yes. That was wrong. I was careless with the category.\""), .cross("The candidate says no van was bought, doesn't {V.he}?", "\"I know. We rented a van, and I bought a car. I should have explained it.\""), .cross("You drove the sedan every day, didn't you?", "\"Yes, to events and to work. I did not separate campaign use from my own.\""), .cross("The candidate never agreed to a purchase, did the candidate?", "\"No. I should have gotten that approval first.\"")],
        openings: ("A campaign treasurer, {D}, paid $31,000 in donations to a car dealership. The invoice shows a sedan titled to {D.him}, and the filing called it signage. The State will present the candidate, the invoice, and the filing.", "The defense will present a campaign that really used a van, a treasurer who kept messy records, and a misunderstanding about a purchase, not a theft."),
        closings: ("$31,000 of donors' money, a sedan titled to the treasurer, and a filing that called it signage. The candidate never approved a vehicle.", "A campaign needed a vehicle, and a careless treasurer filed it badly. The State has not proved {D} meant to take donations for personal use."),
        timeline: [(-90, "Donations arrive."), (0, "The purchase."), (30, "The filing."), (60, "The candidate notices.")],
        identified: "A dealership invoice.",
        aggravating: ["The defendant took advantage of a position of trust or confidence"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "People gave twenty-five and fifty dollars out of their grocery money because they believed in what we were trying to do. When they found out where it had gone, many of them stopped giving to anyone. That's the hardest part for me to accept. Donors trusted us.",
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let foodBankVacations = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.foodBankVacations",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Food Bank Director Charged Personal Vacations to Charity Cards", "$210,000 Over Three Years"],
        law: "embezzlement100k",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Embezzled over $100,000 belonging to {V}, a food bank, by a person in a position of trust, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D}, a food bank director, charged $210,000 in vacations and furniture to charity cards over three years. {DL} says they were fundraising trips. The statements show resort stays and furniture, the calendar shows weekend trips, and the board chair says none were approved.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Card Statements", "Resort stays and furniture."), E(.document, 3, "Calendar", "Trips on weekends."), E(.statement, 2, "Board Chair", "No trips were approved.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Fundraising", "{DL} says they were fundraising trips.")],
        role: "Board chair",
        exam: [.direct("What did you find about the food bank's cards?", "\"Over three years, $210,000 in vacations and furniture charged to charity cards. The statements show resort stays and furniture.\""), .direct("What does the calendar show?", "\"Trips on weekends, matching the resort charges. They don't line up with any food bank events.\""), .direct("Were the trips approved?", "\"No. As board chair, I can say no trips were approved. We never authorized travel on that scale.\""), .direct("What is your role with the food bank?", "\"I chair the board of directors, a volunteer role. We oversee the director and meet every other month.\""), .direct("How was the problem discovered?", "\"A donor asked why the charity's tax return showed large travel and furnishing costs. We hired an auditor, who traced the card statements.\""), .direct("What did the statements show?", "\"Charges at beach resorts, a mountain lodge, and a furniture store, totaling $210,000 over three years. Many were on Friday or Saturday.\""), .cross("{DL} says they were fundraising trips, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Fundraising travel can be legitimate. But there's no record of events or donors tied to those trips.\""), .cross("Did you review the cards monthly?", "\"Not as closely as I should have. We trusted {D}. That's on us.\""), .cross("The board did approve travel in general, didn't it?", "\"We approved a travel budget for conferences and donor visits. It was not for resort weekends.\""), .cross("You reviewed the cards only once a quarter, didn't you?", "\"Yes. We looked at summaries and trusted the director to explain anything unusual.\""), .cross("The board chair signed off on the budget that included travel, didn't they?", "\"The budget had a general travel line. It did not name these trips, these resorts, or the furniture, and no one approved them separately.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Staff accountant",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What is your role at the food bank?", "\"I am the staff accountant. I record card charges, pay vendors, and prepare reports for the board.\""), .direct("How did you code the director's charges?", "\"The travel went under travel and fundraising, and the furniture under equipment. I coded them as presented on receipts.\""), .direct("Did the director attend fundraising events?", "\"Yes, many, including galas and donor dinners. I saw photos in the newsletter.\""), .direct("Did you attach receipts?", "\"Most of the time I filed what the director gave me. The resort bills were itemized when we had them.\""), .direct("What did you do when you noticed large travel totals?", "\"I mentioned them in my monthly report to the director. I was told they were fundraising related and left it there.\""), .direct("Did you ever see a travel approval form?", "\"Not for the resort stays. We did not have a form for that.\""), .cross("Many trips were on weekends, weren't they?", "\"Yes, and I did not check the dates against any events.\""), .cross("You never questioned the furniture charges, did you?", "\"I asked once and was told it was for the office. I did not visit the office to check.\""), .cross("You are responsible for reviewing coding, aren't you?", "\"Yes, and I could have done a better job.\""), .cross("You never told the board about the totals, did you?", "\"I gave summaries. I did not separate out the resorts.\""), .cross("$210,000 is a lot for a food bank, isn't it?", "\"Yes, it is. I did not see how big it was until the auditor added it up.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} used charity cards.", "Fundraising."),
        allocution: "\"Those trips were fundraising trips, meant to build support for the food bank, and I believed I was doing what was needed. I mixed up personal and charity expenses, and I should have kept them apart. I've given my life to feeding people and I regret every dollar that confused it.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} met two donors on one trip.", "The board approved travel in general terms."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you take those trips?", "\"They were fundraising trips. I met people and made connections for the food bank. It was part of building support.\""), .direct("Did you intend to steal from the food bank?", "\"No. I believed I was doing what was needed to raise money. I mixed up personal and charity expenses.\""), .direct("What did you accomplish at the food bank?", "\"I built it from one pantry to three sites and tripled the donated food. I spent nights and weekends on fundraising.\""), .direct("What did one of those trips involve?", "\"I met two donors at a resort and received a pledge from one of them. I used the trip to deepen the relationship.\""), .direct("What about the furniture?", "\"I bought office furniture and a sofa for the volunteer lounge. Some pieces went to my home when I ran out of space.\""), .direct("What did you tell the board about the trips afterward?", "\"I mentioned that I had been meeting donors on the road. I did not give dates or a list, and I wish I had put them in writing.\""), .cross("Resort stays on weekends aren't typical fundraising, are they?", "\"No. I see how it looks. That's when the donors were free.\""), .cross("$210,000 is a lot of fundraising, isn't it?", "\"It is. I can't show that much came in. I should have kept better records.\""), .cross("The board never approved those trips, did it?", "\"Not specifically. I thought general approval covered it. I was wrong.\""), .cross("Weekend resort stays are not donor meetings, are they?", "\"Not all of them were. Some were rest I took after long weeks, and I charged them.\""), .cross("You never submitted trip reports, did you?", "\"No. I should have kept notes of every meeting.\"")],
        openings: ("Over three years, {D}, a food bank director, charged $210,000 in resort stays and furniture to charity cards. Weekend trips fill the calendar, and the board chair says none were approved. The State will show the statements and the calendar.", "Jurors will also see a director who raised money, took trips tied to fundraising, and whose accountant recorded every charge openly. Listen closely to the witnesses."),
        closings: ("Three years, $210,000, resort stays and furniture, and no board approval. The money was meant for food for hungry families, and {D} spent it on trips.", "The charges were recorded openly, and {D} says they supported fundraising. The State has not proved {DL} meant to steal rather than mix up business and personal."),
        timeline: [(-1095, "Charges begin."), (0, "Year 3: audit."), (0, "Year 3: the calendar."), (1, "{DL} resigns.")],
        identified: "Card statements.",
        aggravating: ["The defendant took advantage of a position of trust or confidence"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "Pantries ran short last winter, and we had to turn families away at the door. We cut the canned goods and the fresh produce, and some volunteers gave up. People who rely on us never knew where the money went. They only knew the shelves were bare.",
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let vendingRouteSkim = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.vendingRouteSkim",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Vending Route Driver Reported Less Coin Than Collected", "Sealed Counters Show a Gap"],
        law: "embezzlement",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Embezzled $19,000 belonging to {V}, a vending company, by a person in a position of trust, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A route driver, {D}, reported $19,000 less than machine counters recorded over a year. {DL} says counters were faulty. The gaps began a year earlier. The counters read higher than the deposits, the route sheets were short on {D.his} route, and a warehouse camera shows {DL} pocketing bills.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Counter Logs", "Higher than deposits."), E(.video, 2, "Warehouse Camera", "{D} pockets bills."), E(.document, 2, "Route Sheets", "Short on {D}'s route.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Faulty", "{DL} says counters were faulty.")],
        role: "Route manager",
        exam: [.direct("What did you find in the route records?", "\"$19,000 less in deposits than the machine counters recorded over a year. The gap is on {D}'s route.\""), .direct("What do the counter logs show?", "\"Higher numbers than the deposits. The counters read higher than what was turned in.\""), .direct("How does your route work?", "\"Drivers refill about forty machines each week, collect the cash, and deposit it at the office. Each machine has a counter that records every dollar taken in.\""), .direct("What did the comparison show?", "\"Counters on {D.his} route recorded about $19,000 more than the deposits over a year. The other routes matched their counters within a few dollars.\""), .direct("What did the warehouse camera show?", "\"{D.He} stands at the cash table counting bills, then slips several into a jacket pocket and walks to the lot. It lasts about fifteen seconds.\""), .direct("How do you check a route driver's deposits against the machine counters?", "\"Each week we compare the counter reading to the cash turned in. A small gap is normal, but a gap that repeats on one route week after week is a red flag.\""), .cross("Counters can fail, can't they?", "\"Yes. Two counters had repairs logged, and I cannot argue.\""), .cross("Were the other machines accurate?", "\"Yes. The other machines' counters matched their deposits.\""), .cross("Did {D} buy a motorcycle?", "\"I heard so. I do not know how it was paid for.\""), .cross("A counter can read high when it malfunctions, can't it?", "\"Yes. Two counters on {D.his} route had repairs logged, and that could explain a few hundred dollars.\""), .cross("You cannot say how much was in the jacket, can you?", "\"No. The video does not show denominations.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Technician",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did any of the counters on the route fail?", "\"Two did. I repaired them myself. They were reading wrong for a while before I caught the problem.\""), .direct("What about the other counters on the route?", "\"They were fine. I checked them, and they were accurate. Only two had problems that I could find.\""), .direct("Could those two failures explain $19,000 in missing money?", "\"No, they could not. The amounts do not add up, and the failures lasted only a short time.\""), .direct("What is your job?", "\"I am a service technician who repairs machines and replaces counters across the routes. I carry spare parts and a testing meter.\""), .direct("What did you find on {D}'s route?", "\"Two machines with sticky counters that read high. I replaced both counters the same day.\""), .direct("How long were they faulty?", "\"A few weeks, according to the log. I cannot say exactly when each one began.\""), .cross("How long were the two faulty counters off?", "\"A few weeks at most. Not a year, which is how long the gap in the deposits went on.\""), .cross("Were both of those machines on the defendant's route?", "\"Yes. Both were on {D}'s route. I will not pretend otherwise, and that fact is in my repair log.\""), .cross("Did you check every machine on the defendant's route?", "\"I checked the ones with reported problems. I did not test every machine on the route, I admit.\""), .cross("Two counters cannot explain $19,000, can they?", "\"No. Two counters would account for maybe a few hundred dollars.\""), .cross("You did not test the other machines on that route, did you?", "\"Only the ones with reports. The rest were not flagged.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} skimmed vending cash.", "Faulty counters."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry for the loss. I turned in everything I collected on that route, and I never took money from the machines. The counters were faulty, two of them were repaired, and I believe more were off. I'd ask the court to look carefully at the machines, not just at me.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} bought a motorcycle.", "Two machines had counter repairs logged."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you skim money from the machines?", "\"No. I did not take money from the route. I turned in what I collected.\""), .direct("Why do the counters read higher than the deposits?", "\"The counters were faulty. Two of them were repaired, and I believe more were off.\""), .direct("What about the motorcycle?", "\"I bought it with savings. It had nothing to do with the route.\""), .direct("How did you do your route?", "\"I drove it every week for six years and had very few complaints. I counted cash with a coworker watching when I could.\""), .direct("What did you do with the money on the table?", "\"I counted bills into stacks and kept my own cash for lunch in my pocket. I may have put one of my own twenties in the wrong pocket.\""), .direct("What explains the motorcycle?", "\"I bought it used for $3,500 after saving for two years. I have the title and a bank record.\""), .cross("A camera shows you pocketing bills, doesn't it?", "\"It shows me putting something in my pocket. It was my own cash, I believe.\""), .cross("Two counters were fixed. What about the other $19,000?", "\"I do not know. I think more counters were off.\""), .cross("Only your route was short, wasn't it?", "\"Yes, and I cannot explain why except for the counters.\""), .cross("You have six years of experience with these machines, don't you?", "\"Yes, and I know counters fail from time to time. I do not know why they would all fail on one route.\""), .cross("The deposit sheets from your route do not match the counters, do they?", "\"Not exactly, and I cannot explain every dollar. I know two machines had repairs, but I understand why the rest of the gap looks bad.\"")],
        openings: ("A vending route driver, {D}, turned in $19,000 less than the machine counters recorded over a year. A warehouse camera shows {DL} pocketing bills, and {D.he} bought a motorcycle.", "The defense case is that two counters were faulty, that the camera shows only a pocket, and that {D} paid for the motorcycle with savings."),
        closings: ("A year of short deposits on {D}'s route, counters that read higher, a camera showing bills pocketed, and a new motorcycle. These facts line up.", "Two failing counters and a camera that shows a pocket. The State has numbers on a page, but it has not proved {D} took the money."),
        timeline: [(-365, "Gaps begin."), (0, "Year 1: audit."), (0, "Year 1: the camera."), (1, "{DL} is suspended.")],
        identified: "Counter logs.",
        aggravating: ["The defendant took advantage of a position of trust or confidence"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let fireAuxTreasurer = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.fireAuxTreasurer",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Fire Department Auxiliary Treasurer Covered Personal Debts From the Fund", "Pancake Supper Cash Missing"],
        law: "embezzlement",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Embezzled $14,500 belonging to {V}, a fire department auxiliary, by a person in a position of trust, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "An auxiliary's treasurer, {D}, paid personal bills from a fund raised by pancake suppers. Statements showed $14,500 withdrawn. {DL} says the money was a loan.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Bank Statements", "Withdrawals for {D}'s bills."), E(.document, 2, "Minutes", "No loan approved."), E(.statement, 2, "Member", "'We never voted on a loan.'")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Loan", "{DL} says it was a loan.")],
        role: "Auxiliary president",
        exam: [.direct("What happened to the auxiliary's fund?", "\"It was raised through pancake suppers. Statements show $14,500 withdrawn to pay {D}'s personal bills.\""), .direct("What do the minutes show?", "\"No loan was approved. We keep minutes of every meeting, and nothing about a loan to {DL} appears.\""), .direct("What did members tell you?", "\"They said, 'We never voted on a loan.' I heard that from several members after we found the withdrawals.\""), .direct("How does the auxiliary raise money?", "\"Through monthly pancake suppers at the fire hall, a bake sale, and a spring raffle. We use the money for scholarships and equipment for the volunteer firefighters.\""), .direct("How did you learn about the withdrawals?", "\"A new member asked to see the bank statements at our annual meeting. The statements showed cash withdrawals and card payments to a utility, a car loan, and a department store.\""), .direct("How much was withdrawn in total?", "\"$14,500 over about six months, in amounts from a few hundred to more than a thousand dollars. Only $2,000 had been paid back.\""), .cross("{DL} says it was a loan, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"A loan needs approval, and none was given. I'm not aware of any written loan terms.\""), .cross("Did {DL} ever mention a loan?", "\"Once, I'm told, in passing. It wasn't formally raised at a meeting.\""), .cross("Did {DL} hide the withdrawals?", "\"No. They show on the statements. Anyone checking would have seen them.\""), .cross("The statements are mailed to the treasurer, aren't they?", "\"Yes, and the treasurer reports to us each month. I did not ask for copies until the member brought it up.\""), .cross("{D} did repay some of it, didn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes, $2,000, in two deposits. That still leaves most of it outstanding.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Auxiliary member",
        defenseExam: [.direct("How are you connected to the auxiliary?", "\"I am a longtime member and help at most of the pancake suppers. I serve coffee and wash dishes.\""), .direct("What did {D} tell you?", "\"At a supper in the spring, {D} said something about borrowing a little from the fund until payday. It sounded casual.\""), .direct("What did you understand by that?", "\"That it was a small loan for a few weeks. I did not know it was thousands of dollars.\""), .direct("Did you ask any questions?", "\"No. I assumed the board knew and had agreed. I did not ask who approved it.\""), .direct("How did the defendant act around the group?", "\"Normal, cheerful, and helpful. {D.He} ran the suppers well and was always the first to arrive.\""), .direct("What did you think when you learned of the total?", "\"I was stunned. It was far more than I had pictured, and I felt bad that I had not said something.\""), .cross("There was never any vote on a loan, was there?", "\"None that I attended, and none in the minutes I saw.\""), .cross("You did not tell the president about the comment, did you?", "\"No. I did not think it was my place.\""), .cross("Nothing was in writing, was it?", "\"Nothing that I ever saw.\""), .cross("A casual remark is not an approval, is it?", "\"No. I see that now, and I wish I had asked more.\""), .cross("You cannot say how much the defendant meant to borrow, can you?", "\"No. I only heard a vague phrase at a supper.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took fund money.", "A loan."),
        allocution: "\"I was short that year and I planned to pay it back. I thought of it as a loan from the auxiliary, and I mentioned it once but should have raised it formally. I let it slide, and that was wrong. I'll repay every dollar and apologize to the members.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} repaid $2,000.", "{DL} told one member about a loan."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you withdraw the money?", "\"I was short and planned to pay it back. I thought of it as a loan, and I meant to repay the auxiliary.\""), .direct("Did you tell the members?", "\"I mentioned it once. I should have raised it formally. I let it slide.\""), .direct("Did you intend to steal?", "\"No. I always meant to put it back. I'd never take money from a group I love.\""), .direct("What was your situation that year?", "\"My spouse had lost work and we fell behind on the car loan and utilities. I borrowed from the fund to keep the lights on.\""), .direct("How did you plan to repay?", "\"From my paycheck, a little each month, until the full amount was back. I paid $2,000 in the first two months.\""), .direct("What did you tell people?", "\"I told one member in passing that I was borrowing and would pay it back. I never brought it up at a meeting.\""), .cross("The minutes show no approved loan, don't they?", "\"I know. I never put it to a vote. I was afraid they'd say no.\""), .cross("$14,500 is a lot to borrow without asking, isn't it?", "\"Yes. I know. It was wrong not to ask.\""), .cross("You paid your personal bills with it, didn't you?", "\"Yes. That was the plan. I meant to cover it before anyone noticed.\""), .cross("You did not ask for a vote, did you?", "\"No. I was embarrassed and afraid they would say no.\""), .cross("You spent more than you meant to borrow, didn't you?", "\"Yes. It started small and grew each month, and I lost track of the total.\"")],
        openings: ("An auxiliary's treasurer, {D}, withdrew $14,500 raised through pancake suppers and paid personal bills with it. The minutes show no loan was ever approved. The State will present the president and the statements.", "The defense will point you to a treasurer who always meant to repay, mentioned a loan to a member, and hid nothing on the statements. Listen closely to the witnesses."),
        closings: ("$14,500 raised one pancake supper at a time, spent on {D}'s bills, with no vote and no loan. That is embezzlement from a charity.", "{D} called it a loan, mentioned it, and left every withdrawal in plain sight on the statements. The State has not proved {DL} meant to keep the money."),
        timeline: [(-180, "Withdrawals begin."), (0, "Month 6: audit."), (0, "Month 6: statements."), (1, "{DL} resigns.")],
        identified: "Statements.",
        aggravating: ["The defendant took advantage of a position of trust or confidence"],
        mood: .divided,
        impact: "Our trust was broken. We spent years flipping pancakes and selling tickets to buy equipment for the fire company, and those dollars were ours. When I saw the statements, I couldn't breathe. We're a small town, and everyone's a friend. That's what hurts the most.",
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

