        truths: ("{DL} owned a color printer.", "A bar receipt shows {DL} received change in twenties the night before."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you print the counterfeit bills?", "\"No. I did not print any money. I received those bills as change at a bar.\""), .direct("Where did you get the printer?", "\"I use it for work. I printed forms and flyers on it, and I never printed currency.\""), .direct("Why were the bills in five towns?", "\"I travel a lot. I spent the bills as I went, not knowing they were bad.\""), .direct("How did you get the twenties?", "\"A bartender gave me change in twenties the night before after I paid with a fifty. I have the receipt for the tab.\""), .direct("What do you use the printer for?", "\"Work forms, invoices, and my kid's school projects. I use cheap copy paper from the office supply store.\""), .direct("What did you do with the cash the next day?", "\"I used it for gas, groceries, and a haircut across three towns. I paid without looking at them.\""), .cross("You own a color printer and paper, don't you?", "\"Yes. Lots of people do. I use it for school and work, not for money.\""), .cross("The same serial number appeared on bills in five towns. Isn't that your doing?", "\"I do not know. I only know I got them as change, and I spent them.\""), .cross("You can prove you got them at a bar?", "\"A bar receipt shows I got change in twenties the night before.\""), .cross("You travel for work, and those bills showed up where you went, didn't they?", "\"They did, and that is the part that hurts me. I traveled because my job sends me there.\""), .cross("You never checked the bills when you received them, did you?", "\"No. Nobody checks change at a bar, and I did not either.\"")],
        openings: ("Counterfeit twenties with the same serial number surfaced in five towns, and store cameras show {D} passing bills at three of them. A color printer and paper were found in {D.his} possession.", "The defense will present evidence that {D} received the bills as change at a bar, has a receipt, and travels for work, which explains the five towns."),
        closings: ("One serial number, five towns, three store cameras showing {D}, and a color printer in {D.his} home. These bills did not come from a bar.", "A bar receipt for change in twenties, a printer used for ordinary work, and a traveler who spent bills as {D.he} went. The State must prove {D} knew they were fake."),
