        role: "ER nurse",
        exam: [.direct("What did you notice among the patients who came in?", "\"Three patients arrived with cash missing from their wallets after riding with {D}, a paramedic. One wallet was lighter on arrival.\""), .direct("How did the reports come in?", "\"Reports began two weeks before the third patient. Each had ridden with {D.him}.\""), .direct("How did you notice the missing cash?", "\"Three patients in two weeks told me their wallets were lighter than they remembered. Each had arrived by ambulance on a different night.\""), .direct("What did the ER nurse see on one arrival?", "\"I handled one patient's wallet and found only a few dollars. The patient said they had two hundred when they left home.\""), .direct("What does the ambulance camera show?", "\"{D.He} opens a wallet during a run, looks at the cash, and closes it. The clip does not show money leaving the wallet.\""), .direct("What did the ER do when the second wallet was reported light?", "\"We pulled the intake logs and flagged the three arrival times. The common name on all three runs was the same crew, and that is when we sent it to security.\""), .cross("{D} says staff handled the wallets, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. {D.He} says that inventory is normal, and wallets are bagged and counted.\""), .cross("Was the defendant on all three runs?", "\"Yes. The ER logs list {DL} on all three.\""), .cross("Who bagged the wallets?", "\"The ER logs list wallets bagged by {D.his} partner.\""), .cross("Opening a wallet to inventory is normal, isn't it?", "\"Yes, crews inventory belongings, and the policy calls for two people to count.\""), .cross("Who else was in the ER crew that night?", "\"Two aides and a nurse. The sign-in log lists each of them with the time they came on shift.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Partner paramedic",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Who bagged the wallets on those runs?", "\"Usually me. I put patient belongings in bags and listed them. That is standard in our service.\""), .direct("Were you on all three runs with {D}?", "\"I was there on most runs, and I handled wallets on most of them.\""), .direct("Did the defendant open wallets?", "\"Sometimes, to inventory. We both do. It is how we log what a patient has.\""), .direct("How long have you ridden with the defendant?", "\"About three years on most shifts. I trust {D} with my life on calls.\""), .direct("What does the procedure require?", "\"Two people to witness the count. In a rush, one of us does it and the other bags.\""), .direct("What did you do on those runs?", "\"I bagged the wallets after {DF} handed them to me. I wrote the bag numbers on the sheet.\""), .cross("Did you count the cash yourself?", "\"Not always. Sometimes we just bagged it. I did not count every bill.\""), .cross("Did you see the defendant take money?", "\"No. I did not see that. But I was not watching every minute.\""), .cross("How many runs did you share with the defendant?", "\"Many. We rode together often. I do not think {D.he} would do that.\""), .cross("You did not count the cash each time, did you?", "\"Not always. We trust each other.\""), .cross("You were not looking at the wallet while the defendant had it, were you?", "\"Not the whole time. I was driving and watching the monitor. I trusted the process and did not recount the money.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took cash.", "Others handled."),
        allocution: "\"I'm ashamed that anything like this happened on my watch. I did not take any cash. I opened a wallet to inventory the contents, which is part of the job, and I did it on camera. I've served this community for years, and I'm sorry for the patients' worry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had been on all three runs.", "The ER logs list wallets bagged by {DL}'s partner."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you take cash from patients' wallets?", "\"No. I did not take any cash. I only did inventory, as I always do.\""), .direct("What does the camera show?", "\"Me opening a wallet to inventory the contents. That is part of the job.\""), .direct("Were you on all three runs?", "\"Yes. But so was my partner. My partner bagged the wallets.\""), .direct("What is the inventory procedure on a run?", "\"We open the wallet to note cash, cards, and ID, then bag it and sign for it at the ER. It is a standard step in our training.\""), .direct("What happened on those three runs?", "\"I opened the wallet, counted quickly, and passed it to my partner to bag. I did not take any cash.\""), .direct("How did you learn of the complaints?", "\"My supervisor called me in after the third report and told me about it. I was suspended that day.\""), .cross("Three patients lost cash on your runs, didn't they?", "\"Yes. I do not know how. I was doing my job.\""), .cross("One wallet was lighter on arrival at the ER. Who had it?", "\"I opened it for inventory. I did not take any money.\""), .cross("Your partner bagged the wallets. Are you blaming your partner?", "\"I am not blaming anyone. I am saying I did not do it.\""), .cross("You worked all three runs, didn't you?", "\"Yes. So did my partner, and others were in the ER.\""), .cross("You counted the cash alone, didn't you?", "\"Sometimes, when the patient was unstable. I know that is not ideal.\"")],
        openings: ("Three patients arrived at an ER with cash missing from their wallets after ambulance rides with {D}, a paramedic. An ambulance camera shows {DL} opening a wallet, and an ER nurse says one wallet was lighter on arrival.", "By the end of this trial, the proof will show that opening wallets is part of inventory, that {D}'s partner usually bagged them, and that nobody saw {DL} take any cash."),
        closings: ("Three patients, three rides with {D}, a camera showing a wallet opened, and cash missing each time. That is not a coincidence.", "An ambulance crew that inventories wallets and a partner who bagged them. The State has no one who saw {D} take a dollar."),
